# Vercel AI Gateway configuration for /api/audit
# On Vercel deployments: AI Gateway uses OIDC for auth (no provider keys needed).
# For local development: run `vercel env pull` to get env vars, or set AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY.
# Enable AI Gateway in project settings: https://vercel.com/dashboard → Project Settings → AI
#
# Optional: Override the default model (openai/gpt-5.4) for audit generation.
# AUDIT_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.4
# AUDIT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6
#
# Optional: AI Gateway API key for local development (not needed on Vercel deployments).
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Google Places API (New). Used by /api/audit to pull real Google Business
# Profile data (rating, review count, categories, photos) for the business
# being audited. Optional — the audit still runs without it, just with less
# accuracy. Get a key at https://console.cloud.google.com/ → APIs → Places API.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Upstash Redis (via Vercel Marketplace) for persistent rate limiting.
# The Marketplace integration sets these automatically. KV_* names are
# the legacy Vercel KV variables; UPSTASH_* are the current names — either works.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
